WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.385 --> 00:00:16.930
Winter came to an end, and Heidi and Grandfather moved back up the mountain at the first sign

2
00:00:16.950 --> 00:00:17.450
of spring.

3
00:00:18.591 --> 00:00:24.337
The snow had disappeared, and the mountain flowers were already showing their bright heads above the grass.

4
00:00:25.498 --> 00:00:27.360
Heidi was happy to be at home again.

5
00:00:29.844 --> 00:00:34.545
She danced with all the little beetles and winged insects that jumped and crawled in the sun.

6
00:00:35.666 --> 00:00:41.407
She imagined that the tiny creatures were as happy as she and that their chirping voices were singing,

7
00:00:41.427 --> 00:00:43.268
"On the mountain!

8
00:00:43.708 --> 00:00:44.388
On the mountain!"

9
00:00:46.308 --> 00:00:50.090
Late one spring afternoon, Peter arrived from his day up the mountain.

10
00:00:51.290 --> 00:00:56.771
He pushed his way through the goats to hand Heidi a letter, which he had forgotten to deliver

11
00:00:56.811 --> 00:00:57.371
that morning.

12
00:00:58.432 --> 00:01:00.401
When she saw it, Heidi was thrilled.

13
00:01:00.421 --> 00:01:03.784
"It's from Frankfurt, it's from Clara!"

14
00:01:04.064 --> 00:01:04.544
she said.

15
00:01:06.426 --> 00:01:08.267
She opened it and read it aloud.

16
00:01:09.629 --> 00:01:13.672
Clara was well enough to visit, and she and Grandmamma were on their way.

17
00:01:13.692 --> 00:01:17.135
"I can hardly wait," said Heidi.

18
00:01:17.155 --> 00:01:19.837
"Clara and Grandmamma!

19
00:01:20.177 --> 00:01:21.719
How much fun we will have!"

20
00:01:23.440 --> 00:01:24.982
Peter was not very convinced.

21
00:01:26.143 --> 00:01:29.537
Every time Heidi had a visitor, she spent less time with him.

22
00:01:30.697 --> 00:01:36.599
Peter suddenly jumped up and chased the goats at full speed down the mountain, but Heidi was too

23
00:01:36.680 --> 00:01:38.180
happy to notice Peter's mood.

24
00:01:39.301 --> 00:01:43.442
The days went by, and Heidi and Grandfather prepared their house for their guests.

25
00:01:45.483 --> 00:01:51.145
The sound of sawing and chopping came from behind the hut as Grandfather made chairs for their new

26
00:01:51.185 --> 00:01:53.246
visitors with his skillful hands.

27
00:01:54.387 --> 00:01:59.792
On a day that felt as if spring had finally turned to summer, Heidi looked down the mountain

28
00:01:59.832 --> 00:02:04.134
and cried, "Grandfather, Grandfather, come look!"

29
00:02:06.014 --> 00:02:08.575
A strange procession was making its way up the mountain.

30
00:02:09.795 --> 00:02:15.517
In front, two men carried between them a chair on poles, and in it sat a girl, very

31
00:02:15.597 --> 00:02:16.597
carefully wrapped up.

32
00:02:17.797 --> 00:02:24.459
A handsome woman followed, riding on a horse and looking with wonder at the surrounding mountainside.

33
00:02:26.540 --> 00:02:31.227
Finally, another man pushed an empty wheelchair, piled with a bundle of blankets.

34
00:02:31.247 --> 00:02:34.510
"Here they come, here they come!"

35
00:02:35.031 --> 00:02:36.952
shouted Heidi, jumping with joy.

36
00:02:37.933 --> 00:02:43.618
When the procession arrived, Heidi rushed forward, and the two girls embraced each other with delight.

37
00:02:45.079 --> 00:02:49.582
Grandmamma got down from her horse and gave Heidi an affectionate greeting as well.

38
00:02:49.602 --> 00:02:57.292
"What a magnificent residence you have, Grandfather," said Grandmamma.

39
00:02:57.312 --> 00:03:01.553
"I don't know which way to look first, it is all so beautiful.

40
00:03:02.754 --> 00:03:05.274
What do you say, Clara, what do you say?"

41
00:03:07.075 --> 00:03:09.215
Clara gazed around her with amazement.

42
00:03:10.256 --> 00:03:13.937
She had never imagined, much less seen, anything so splendid.

43
00:03:13.957 --> 00:03:19.018
"I can hardly believe how beautiful it all is," she said.

44
00:03:20.118 --> 00:03:26.384
They settled Clara into her wheelchair, and Heidi wheeled her around to show her the fir trees and

45
00:03:26.424 --> 00:03:27.184
the goats' shed.

46
00:03:29.185 --> 00:03:34.728
It wasn't easy to push the chair, but Heidi used all her might and managed to give Clara

47
00:03:34.848 --> 00:03:35.528
a full tour.

48
00:03:35.548 --> 00:03:43.251
"Oh, Heidi, if only I could walk, you could show me everything on the mountain," said Clara, a

49
00:03:43.291 --> 00:03:44.092
little sadly.

50
00:03:45.993 --> 00:03:52.736
While the girls were looking around and talking, Grandmamma and Grandfather got to know one another and set

51
00:03:52.796 --> 00:03:53.436
out the supper.

52
00:03:54.592 --> 00:04:00.615
Grandfather brought out the new chairs, and soon, they were all sitting down to a nice meal on

53
00:04:00.635 --> 00:04:01.575
the mountainside.

54
00:04:03.876 --> 00:04:11.019
After the meal, Grandfather appeared from the shed, carrying two bowls of goat's milk, one for Heidi and

55
00:04:11.119 --> 00:04:11.859
one for Clara.

56
00:04:13.100 --> 00:04:16.881
Clara had never tasted goat's milk before and found it delicious.

57
00:04:16.901 --> 00:04:22.804
"Tomorrow, we will drink two bowls," said Grandfather with satisfaction.

58
00:04:24.480 --> 00:04:30.885
The time passed happily, then Grandmamma said, "We must get ready to go, Clara.

59
00:04:31.985 --> 00:04:37.889
The sun is going down and the men will be here to carry you down to Dorfli soon."

60
00:04:39.050 --> 00:04:41.672
Clara looked up at the cloudless sky over the hut.

61
00:04:41.692 --> 00:04:47.276
"Oh, Grandmamma," she said, "I would like to stay here forever."
